BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Social Reading Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260421T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260421T203000
UID:blogto-233711@blogto.com
DESCRIPTION:We've noticed that people want to read more books\, be social\
 , and get out of the house. Join Quiet Smile at Wildhearts Cafe for a Quie
 t Offline Reading Party\, with an optional book swap.\nLeave your phone ou
 t of reach. Quiet reading time in a room with other people doing the same.
  Pick up that book you keep putting off.\nWhat to expect:\n• Uninterrupt
 ed time to read the book you keep meaning to start or finish.\n• A simpl
 e path into conversation\, with no rush and no pressure.\n• A cozy café
  atmosphere that makes it easier to slow down.\n• Proper time offline\, 
 not just "less online."\nWildhearts Cafe is hosting us to support the miss
 ion. Please leave outside drinks and snacks at home and encourage guests t
 o purchase something from the café.\n6:00 to 6:30 pm: Arrive and settle i
 n\n6:30 to 8:00 pm: Quiet reading time\n8:00 to 8:30 pm: Optional connecti
 on time and book swap\n8:30 pm: Wrap-up\nDive into any book. Bring your ow
 n book\, poetry\, essays\, comics\, steamy fan-fic\, whatever holds your a
 ttention.\nAfter reading\, you can talk with others if you feel like it. T
 his is a low-stakes space where saying hello is normal again\, and nobody 
 needs a clever opening line.\nThe book swap is optional. Bring a finished 
 book that is gathering dust and give it a second life. You might go home w
 ith a new read and the quiet satisfaction of passing something along.
LOCATION:Wildhearts Cafe
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/social-reading-night-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Division
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260421T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260421T213500
UID:blogto-232804@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/28/original_image87cec1b9-4262-4c4a-8bf8-7be6949dd2
 87.jpg
DESCRIPTION:From award-winning Ukrainian Canadian writer/director Andrew K
 ushnir\, The Division puzzles through a family history shaped by war – a
 nd what gets carried forward into today’s battle.\nAfter publishing a eu
 logy for his renowned watchmaker grandfather in a national newspaper\, And
 rew is confronted by an accusation in the comments section. The charge sen
 ds him on a 19\,000-kilometre journey through Ukraine and Europe with daun
 ting questions—and the rare timepiece he's inherited. Retracing his gran
 dfather’s footsteps as a soldier and immigrant\, he unearths a family my
 thology that has astonishing implications for the present.\nIn a landscape
  where history is both weapon and wound\, Andrew’s search pulls him deep
  into the stories of a shrinking Ukrainian village\, into the fallout of R
 ussia’s full-scale invasion\, and into the silence of the dead.\nOrigina
 lly featured at Lincoln Center\, NYC\, The Division is a gripping new work
  on identity\, legacy\, and the slyness of memory. With his acclaimed blen
 d of documentary theatre and deeply personal storytelling\, Kushnir faces 
 the unspoken truths that shape both our individual and collective historie
 s — and our here and now.
LOCATION:Crow's Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/the-division-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
