SUMMARY:Mindful Spaces: A Creative Journey through Architecture
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260424T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260424T170000
UID:blogto-233808@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/17/original_imageff468e99-6a26-4d5f-b65a-ba9ff2c09d
 e8.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Focus on how architectural environments shape our inner experi
 ence. The architecture of the Royal Ontario Museum is exquisite. It spans 
 Neo-Romanesque\, Neo- Byzantine\, Art Deco\, Modernist and Deconstructivis
 t styles\, with some spaces combining multiple designs. On this mindfulnes
 s journey\, participants will be led through four unique architectural loc
 ations in the Museum that spark a sense of awe\, curiosity\, and beauty.\n
 Participants will be creatively guided on how to connect to their senses i
 n each location\, and then to their own personal inner world. Leaning into
  carefully selected themes\, and allowing personal associations and meanin
 gful memories to emerge\, participants will explore how architecture\, the
 ir senses\, and their own creativity can nourish a mindfulness awareness\,
  allow for grounding\, and inspire self-discovery.
LOCATION:Royal Ontario Museum
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/mindful-spaces-a-creative-journey-throug
 h-architecture-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
