BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Ambient Evening at St. Anne's: Jessica Moss & Pursuit Grooves &
  Nick Schofield & Kilometre Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260425T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260425T223000
UID:blogto-233328@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/08/original_image92ff76fa-31ee-425e-8a51-d0b28a2fa3
 4c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented with Sonic Boom\nIn partnership with TO Live\nCo-pre
 sented with Imaginary North Records\nJESSICA MOSS\n(Montréal // Constella
 tion Records // immersive violin loops)\nwith:\nPURSUIT GROOVES (Toronto /
 / experimental electronic travels)\nNICK SCHOFIELD (Gatineau // Backward M
 usic // Blue Hour ambient jazz album release)\nKILOMETRE CLUB (Toronto // 
 Imaginary North + Nettwerk Records // prolific soundscape creator + field 
 recorder)\nPart of the Wavelength Music Series\nSaturday April 25\, 2026\n
 Wavelength @ St. Anne’s\n651 Dufferin Street\nDoors 6pm\nSingle tix $26 
 adv plus taxes & fees at DICE.FM\nChildren under 12 free when accompanied 
 by an adult!\nTicket link: https://bit.ly/AmbientAnnes\nOn sale now!\nALL 
 AGES / Licensed\nGet cozy and be ready to be transported! This ambient eve
 ning promises to loop your mind forwards and back\, with textures crunchin
 g under your toes and wiggling in your ears.\nThis line-up is an exchange 
 between sonic experimenters from Québec and Ontario\, bringing decades of
  experience\, field recordings\, and innovative technology to Wavelength
 ’s monthly music series. Expect the bells and whistles\, soul and bass\,
  and stillness and intensity from our ambient ambassadors!\nCo-presented w
 ith Imaginary North Records (aka Kilometre Club aka Daniel Field)\, we can
 ’t wait to immerse you in pure sound at our home base @ St. Anne’s. Th
 is will be the perfect chillout comedown after the hectic Wavelength festi
 val weekend in March. Expect visual decor by resident WL artists to truly 
 take you away!\nAccessibility\nSt. Anne’s Parish Hall is not currently w
 heelchair accessible due to one flight of stairs to access the venue. If y
 ou have accessibility needs\, don’t hesitate to contact us at info@wavel
 engthmusic.ca.\nAudience Policy\nWavelength respects the rights of each me
 mber of our diverse audience and is committed to providing an environment 
 in which everyone can feel safe. Any behaviour which could reasonably be p
 erceived as physically\, emotionally\, or mentally harmful to individuals 
 at Wavelength events will not be tolerated. This includes: racism\, sexism
 \, homophobia\, transphobia\, body shaming\, ableism\, ageism\, and all fo
 rms of violence.\nPlease be respectful of others and help Wavelength creat
 e a fun and safer space for everyone. If you need help\, or see others in 
 need of help\, please talk to a Wavelength staff member.
LOCATION:Wavelength @ St. Anne's
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/an-ambient-evening-at-st-annes-jessica-m
 oss-pursuit-grooves-nick-schofield-kilometre-club-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
