BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:HOMECOMING Group Exhibition Inside a Laundromat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260425T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260425T210000
UID:blogto-233644@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/14/original_image9870a923-94ef-4c8a-9bad-802a85ea06
 81.jpg
DESCRIPTION:"Homecoming" is a group exhibition opening April 25 in Toronto
 \, presented by Vytik Art Collective at She Said Gallery - a project space
  embedded within a working laundromat. The show brings together 8 artists 
 exploring ideas of return\, memory\, and belonging across a range of media
 .\nSet within the everyday rhythms of a laundromat\, the exhibition draws 
 a parallel between cycles of washing\, waiting\, and repetition\, and the 
 ways we revisit the past and reconstruct a sense of 'home'. The setting an
 d curatorial approach offer a more intimate and unconventional exhibition 
 format\, situating contemporary art within a lived\, transitional space.\n
 Exhibition Name: HOMECOMING Group Exhibition\nOpening Reception: Saturday\
 , April 25\, 6-9 pm\nLocation: She Said Gallery\, 384 Roncesvalles Ave\, T
 oronto\nTickets (free): https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/homecoming-group-exhib
 ition-by-vytik-art-collective-tickets-1987403973785?utm-campaign=social&ut
 m-content=attendeeshare&utm-medium=discovery&utm-term=listing&utm-source=c
 p&aff=ebdsshcopyurl\nExhibition Statement: “Homecoming” brings togethe
 r 8 artists working across a range of media\, reflecting on the act of ret
 urn - both physical and emotional. The exhibition approaches ‘home’ no
 t as a fixed destination\, but as something continually reassembled throug
 h memory\, distance\, and lived experience.\nPresented inside She Said Gal
 lery\, a project space embedded within a working laundromat in Toronto\, t
 he exhibition unfolds within a setting shaped by everyday rhythms. Here\, 
 cycles of washing\, waiting\, and folding mirror the quiet processes throu
 gh which we revisit the past and piece together fragments of belonging.\nB
 etween movement and stillness\, departure and return\, “Homecoming” co
 nsiders how the idea of home persists across geographies\, objects\, and r
 elationships - constantly shifting\, yet deeply felt.\nEvent Sponsors: Jun
 ction Craft Brewery and Woodhouse Brewing.\nExhibition Dates: April 25 - A
 pril 30\, 2026.\nMusic and live painting at the opening reception!
LOCATION:She Said Gallery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/homecoming-group-exhibition-inside-a-lau
 ndromat-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
