 gto.com/events/2026/03/24/original_image77331faa-db3c-4725-bea2-6cb95722e2
 86.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Bars look social from the outside\, but most people just stick
  to the group they came with. It’s surprisingly hard to meet anyone new 
 in public spaces.\nAt It’s in the Cards\, talking to other people is the
  whole point. You get a card when you arrive and trade it throughout the n
 ight to try and get the one you want. It’s all in good fun and designed 
 to create conversation\, so talking to people you don’t know is not only
  allowed\, it’s expected and easy.\nAt the end of the night\, we do a dr
 aw where 1 in 3 people win a real gift card to the place they’re holding
 \, so make sure it’s somewhere you like.\nDesigned for those aged 30 and
  up. Everyone 19+ is welcome.\nApril 25\, 7:00 PM to 10:00 PM\nLiberty Vil
 lage (private event space)\nTickets: $35 early bird (includes a drink)\, $
 45 regular
LOCATION:Private event space in Liberty Village
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/its-in-the-cards-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
