BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open Studio
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T203000
UID:blogto-233061@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/02/original_imagefe9d3e2d-8050-4d49-b727-ea2b0311d0
 26.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Open Studio\, a space to explore your creativity\,
  connect with others\, and simply create without judgment. Whether you wan
 t to doodle\, colour\, write\, or just relax\, this is your time to do wha
 t inspires you\, alongside like-minded folks.\n​​​Open Studio is mor
 e than a creative outlet. It’s a place to find rest\, connection\, and a
  little relief from daily pressures—a communal experience rooted in care
  and play.\n​​​A portion of proceeds from each will be donated to th
 e Parkdale Food Bank\, supporting nourishment and community care in our ne
 ighbourhood.\n​​​Let’s create together.\n​​​About Re-Work\n
 ​Re-Work is a Community First\n​We're a professional (and personal) de
 velopment community helping people redefine work\, ambition\, and success 
 on their own terms. We want you to get to a healthier\, less stress-filled
  place with the thing we spend most of our lives doing: working. Move beyo
 nd burnout toward work that is meaningful and fulfilling as your fullest s
 elf. Through a proven process and framework\, we help you craft a more sus
 tainable and values-aligned relationship with work. Through workshops\, st
 orytelling\, and community spaces\, Re-Work invites you to explore a healt
 hier\, more sustainable way of working and living.\n​\nLet’s build a f
 uture of work that works for you.
LOCATION:Issues Magazine Shop
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/open-studio-toronto-3/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pascuala Ilabaca & Fauna
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T220000
UID:blogto-233958@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/21/original_image6eeb5f73-ea8b-4698-90bc-3b312b1421
 4c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Accordion-wielding Chilean songstress Pascuala Ilabaca is a tr
 ue hidden gem. A favourite on the vibrant scene of young Chilean singer-so
 ngwriters\, her music is rooted in traditional sounds but effortlessly int
 egrates shades of jazz\, pop\, and rock\, with influences gathered from pl
 aces as distant as India and Mexico.\nAccompanied by her formidable band F
 auna\, Ilabaca’s unique stage presence conjures up sweetness and empower
 ment while simultaneously setting her songs alive with both fragility and 
 verve. Her performance bridges the folkloric roots of the Andes with a con
 temporary global edge.\nAbout the Artist: Pascuala Ilabaca is a singer-son
 gwriter hailing from Valparaiso\, Chile. Her debut album\, Pascuala Canta 
 a Violeta\, was released in 2008\, featuring her arrangements of legendary
  singer-songwriter Violeta Parra’s songs.\nIn 2010\, Ilabaca received th
 e Guitarpin de Oro prize at the Festival del Huaso de Olmué\, and by 2012
 \, she had completed her first two European tours. In 2013\, Ilabaca and h
 er band Fauna were the Audience Award winners for Best World Beat Album at
  the Independent Music Awards. They have graced prestigious stages worldwi
 de\, including the Music and Politics Festival in Berlin\, Barnasants Fest
 ival in Barcelona\, and the London Jazz Festival.\nHer career reached new 
 heights in 2016 when she received the Pulsar Prize \, the most important C
 hilean music industry award. Following the release of her acclaimed album 
 El mito de la pergola in 2018\, she has spent the last several years touri
 ng extensively across Chile\, Europe\, Colombia\, and the United States\, 
 solidifying her reputation as one of the most unique and treasured voices 
 in the Latin American and global music scenes.\nTickets are general admiss
 ion and do not guarantee seating. For Lula dining reservations\, please vi
 sit https://www.lula.ca/reservations\nDoors open at 7:00 pm\nFor general i
 nquiries or accessibility requests\, please email us at boxoffice@smallwor
 ldmusic.com or call us at 416-536-5439.\nThe 2026 Small World Music Series
  is sponsored by TD Bank Group through the TD Ready Commitment and funded 
 by the Government of Canada\, Canada Council for the Arts\, Ontario Arts C
 ouncil\, and the City of Toronto through the Toronto Arts Council.
LOCATION:Lula Lounge
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/pascuala-ilabaca-fauna-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
