BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rendition\, Mayworks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T210000
UID:blogto-233887@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/20/original_image5742b4bb-c2d7-4e62-b8a6-60014aad83
 ad.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A cinematic essay by Euridice Zaituna Kala\, presented as part
  of Every Worker Should Have Equal Labour Rights\, in collaboration with C
 harles Street Video\nExhibition dates are Wednesdays 12-4pm\, Thursdays an
 d Fridays 6-8pm\, Saturday 1-4pm.\nRendition is a hybrid cinematic essay t
 hat questions the documentation of “history in the making” by assembli
 ng a mosaic of materials-from personal memories and interviews to ongoing 
 protest documentation to tell the story of the Madgermans\, a group of con
 tract workers from Mozambique who\, in 1979\, emigrated to East Germany an
 d then abruptly were sent back home upon the reunification of Germany in 1
 989. They have yet to receive the balance of their wages and have turned t
 heir plight into a decades long public demonstration and powerful politica
 l forum.\nRegister at mayworks.ca
LOCATION:Charles Street Video
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/rendition-mayworks-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
