BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:To Hold A Mountain
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T171500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260502T193000
UID:blogto-233204@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/06/original_imagecc01fe4b-9b9c-44bb-b98d-fe08b01905
 d3.jpg
DESCRIPTION:From April 23 to May 3\, the 2026 Hot Docs Festival will prese
 nt documentaries from around the world to audiences in Toronto. 115 films 
 from 51 countries will screen during this year's Festival. Tickets are on 
 sale now.\nIn the quiet\, remote mountains of Montenegro\, Gara and her da
 ughter Nada get by tending to the goats and cows that graze the land. Ever
 y summer\, the pair return to the pasture\, respectfully cherishing the na
 ture that surrounds them. Now\, their traditional way of life is faced wit
 h a potential threat: this land they rely on may be taken over as a traini
 ng ground for NATO troops. For those who live in the Balkan region\, NATO 
 inspires fear\; its history is one of immense loss and devastation. The ju
 xtaposition of the peacefulness of the mountain her people call Mother and
  the contrasting aggression of the military organization sees Gara become 
 an unlikely leader of a campaign to unite her fellow farmers in defiance o
 f the NATO plan. Her battle is about protecting both the land that is sacr
 ed to her and her daughter—the two things she holds closest to her heart
 . Gabor Pertic
LOCATION:TIFF Lightbox
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/to-hold-a-mountain-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
