  Singapore\, Toronto\, Wuppertal and Montréal Symphony Orchestras. As a s
 ought-after soloist\, Kerson has appeared at Carnegie and Wigmore Halls\, 
 Auditorium du Louvre\, and National Center for the Performing Arts\, Beiji
 ng. He plays the ‘ex Bohrer\, Baumgartner’ Guarneri del Gesu violin co
 urtesy of Canimex Inc. Drummondville.\nHis virtuosic recital includes viol
 in works by Ysaÿe (Sonata No. 3 “Ballade” & Sonata No. 4 in E minor)\
 , Kreisler’s Recitativo and Scherzo\, and Bach’s Chaconne from Partita
  No. 2.\nTickets: $70A\, $65Sr\, $40 under 30
