BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Opening Reception - BEING SCENE 25th Annual Juried Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T200000
UID:blogto-233422@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/10/original_image06752a06-f888-459a-a81b-8b0066022f
 b0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Workman Arts celebrates 25 Years of Being Scene with a landmar
 k Exhibition\, opening May 7 and running through June 14\, 2026.\nJoin us 
 for the opening reception of the exhibition on Thursday\, May 7th from 6-8
  PM at our gallery space in 32 Lisgar St (2nd Floor\, Toronto\, ON)\nMarki
 ng a quarter-century of artistic excellence and community impact\, Being S
 cene is a vital platform showcasing the work of artists with lived experie
 nces of mental health and addiction. The artworks on display at this year
 ’s juried exhibition include a diverse collection of painting\, photogra
 phy\, digital media\, installations\, sculpture and video featuring 29 sel
 ect artists. A tailored public program will include Open Studio and other 
 programs/events offered throughout the year.\nBeing Scene represents a sus
 tained commitment to amplifying voices that are too often underrepresented
  in the contemporary landscape. For 25 years\, this exhibition has evolved
  into a key must-attend event on Toronto’s cultural calendar.\nWe are ex
 cited to announce our partnership with Gallery 44\, launching Being Scene 
 x G44 MAD FOCUS annual award presented to recognize excellence and artisti
 c rigor in photography and digital media. The inaugural recipient of this 
 award is Alino Giraldi.\nThe exhibition also honors the legacy of Ica Pas 
 through the awarding of scholarships to Leeay Aikawa and Michael Alemayehu
 .\nThe participating artists were selected by a jury committee of professi
 onal curators from Toronto and Montreal: Simon Cole (Founder and Director 
 – Cooper Cole Gallery)\, Eli Kerr (Founder of Galerie Eli Kerr) and Ann 
 MacDonald (Director and Curator – Doris McCarthy Gallery).
LOCATION:32 Lisgar St
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/opening-reception-being-scene-25th-annua
 l-juried-exhibition-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Operations\, Mayworks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T210000
UID:blogto-233908@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/20/original_image40f861eb-c1f8-4c76-b42c-d5ae59bd24
 f5.jpg
DESCRIPTION:An exhibit by Ibrahim Abusitta\, presented with Whippersnapper
  Gallery\nOperations is an ongoing project by the artist where video foota
 ge of Palestinian resistance is redrawn\, frame by frame\, as a hand-drawn
  animation. By recreating each image on paper by hand\, the work transform
 s footage that would never be shown in legacy media into something tactile
  and enduring. The project explores how we see and process images of the s
 truggle\, creating a space to slow down and reflect on what is routinely e
 rased or left unseen.\nGallery Hours: Saturdays 12-2pm\, Sundays 12-2pm\nO
 pening Reception: Thursday May 7\, 6-9pm\nArtist Talk: The artist will par
 ticipate in a post screening discussion on Thursday May 14\, 7-9pm\nCineCy
 cle\, 129 Spadina Ave\, Toronto\nThis venue is wheelchair accessible and h
 as a gender neutral\, wheelchair accessible washroom. Register at mayworks
 .ca.
LOCATION:CineCycle
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/operations-mayworks-toronto-2/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
