BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Carabao\, Mayworks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T210000
UID:blogto-233893@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/20/original_imagefd71d188-28bc-4e27-8953-677ee8c936
 b0.jpg
DESCRIPTION:By Roann Enriquez\, developed through Mayworks’ Labour Art C
 atalyst in partnership with Anakbayan Toronto\, and informed by research i
 nterviews conducted with Migrante Ontario\, presented in collaboration wit
 h Tarragon Theatre.\nCarabao is a play in development depicting the trials
  and tribulations of a Filipino family across borders\, from Manila and Ca
 buyao City to Toronto and Thunder Bay. Inspired by the historic 74-hour st
 rike at Nexperia Philippines Inc. in March 2025\, the play also addresses 
 illegal recruitment and labour trafficking of Filipino migrant workers int
 o Canada – commonly practiced by unscrupulous agencies amidst rising ant
 i-immigration sentiments around the world. This work of issue-based theatr
 e allows audiences to reflect on the contributions of everyday Filipinos i
 n the workplace – from Chinese-owned manufacturing facilities to Canada
 ’s long-term care homes – as well as on the power of collective action
  in the global labour struggle for workers.\nThe script will be workshoppe
 d with a director and actors over two days. A final read through will be o
 pen to the public at the end of each day\, followed by a Q&A with the play
 wright and Anakbayan Toronto.\nRegister at mayworks.ca\nThis venue is whee
 lchair accessible and has gender neutral\, wheelchair accessible washrooms
 .
LOCATION:Tarragon Theatre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/carabao-mayworks-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
