BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:True North\, 2025\, Mayworks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T220000
UID:blogto-233892@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/20/original_image67a2d3ed-991c-476a-989d-061cb03858
 a6.jpg
DESCRIPTION:96 minutes | USA\, Canada | English and French with English su
 btitles.\nA film by Michèle Stephenson\, presented with U of T Community 
 Engaged Learning Program (New College) the Centre for Caribbean Studies\, 
 and the Caribbean Solidarity Network\nThe film will be followed by a conve
 rsation with the filmmaker where she will speak to her artistic\npractice 
 as a Black liberation project of which True North is a crucial contributio
 n\, and elaborate on the role of narratives in our collective work towards
  liberation.\nIn 1969\, at Montreal’s Concordia University\, a student u
 prising marks itself in the Black liberation movement and sheds light on t
 he often-overlooked history of anti-Black racism in Canada. True North tel
 ls this story of systemic discrimination through archival footage and inti
 mate interviews from former student protestors as well as the West Indians
  who migrated north seeking opportunity and refuge. This film is a testame
 nt to the courage and need for collectivist power.\nRegister at mayworks.c
 a\nThis venue is wheelchair accessible and has gender neutral\, wheelchair
  accessible washrooms.
LOCATION:United Steelworkers Hall
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/true-north-2025-mayworks-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
