ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/14/original_image97e7e6f3-561e-450b-b622-5ea7029429
 73.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate World Migratory Bird Day on May 9th with an early mo
 rning guided bird walk at your Toronto Zoo.\nLed by our knowledgeable guid
 es\, Nigel Parr and Alexandra Israel\, the walk will run from 7:00 AM to 9
 :00 AM. Meet your guides at the front gate for exclusive access and tour t
 hrough the core woods—perfect for spotting songbirds—and along the Eur
 asia loop\, known for its waterfowl.\nLearn about the importance of citize
 n science to bird conservation as we discuss this year’s theme: Every Bi
 rd Counts - Your Observations Matter! Proceeds from the tour will go to th
 e Association of Zoos and Aquariums’ North American Songbirds SAFE progr
 am\, which supports local songbird conservation initiatives. Binoculars wi
 ll be provided\, so just bring your enthusiasm for birdwatching!\nPlease n
 ote: Tour participants will not be charged for parking if they exit the pa
 rking lots prior to 9:30 am. Tour fee does not include parking or admissio
 n to the Zoo for the day. Participants will exit the Zoo prior to opening 
 and may purchase admission to re-enter the Zoo for the day. No member disc
 ount is applicable for this program.
LOCATION:Toronto Zoo
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/toronto-zoo-migratory-bird-day-morning-b
 irding-tour-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
