BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Abendmusik: from Buxtehude to Bach
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260515T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260515T210000
UID:blogto-233749@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/16/original_image0e3e5063-4386-4ee8-b485-b80452e105
 16.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Experience Buxtehude’s profound influence on Bach\nIn 1705\,
  the 20-year-old Johann Sebastian Bach journeyed 400 kilometres on foot fr
 om Arnstadt to Lübeck to meet and learn from the great composer Dietrich 
 Buxtehude\, then aged 70. During Bach’s three-month stay he would have e
 xperienced Buxtehude’s legendary Abendmusiken\, or “Evening Concer
 ts”\, with their mix of sacred vocal and instrumental music presented in
  St. Mary’s Church.\nOur own special Abendmusik invites you to exper
 ience Buxtehude’s profound influence on Bach\, and meet other musical tr
 avellers along the way: Johann Christoph Bach\, Graupner\, Doles\, Reincke
 n and Krebs.\nCome\, refresh your spirit and soul with our Abendmusik 
 offering\, featuring the Tafelmusik Chamber Choir and members of the Tafel
 musik Baroque Orchestra. Buy your tickets for Abendmusik: from Buxtehude t
 o Bach on May 15\, 2026 at tafelmusik.org
LOCATION:Jeanne Lamon Hall\, Trinity-St. Paul’s Centre
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/abendmusik-from-buxtehude-to-bach-toront
 o/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
