BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:From the Ground Up: The PATH and Pedestrian Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260526T193000
UID:blogto-233856@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/19/original_image176a7eee-8c81-46a5-96b7-26b671abfc
 3e.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Beneath Toronto's downtown streets lies one of the world's lar
 gest underground pedestrian networks\, where 30 kilometres of tunnels\, co
 ncourses\, and connections that quietly shape how hundreds of thousands of
  people move through the city every day.\nIn this inaugural tour series\, 
 the Council on Vertical Urbanism's Canada Office welcomes James Parakh\, U
 rban Design Manager for Toronto & East York\, to guide participants throug
 h the history\, design\, and ongoing evolution of the PATH network and Tor
 onto's broader pedestrian realm.\nStarting from City Hall's public plaza\,
  the tour traces how underground infrastructure\, street-level design\, an
 d the spaces between buildings come together to define the experience of t
 he city at ground level. Whether you're a longtime Torontonian or new to t
 he city\, this is a chance to see the urban fabric from a perspective that
  rarely gets the spotlight: from the ground up.\nThis tour will meet in fr
 ont of the main entrance to Toronto City Hall\, 100 Queen Street West.
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/from-the-ground-up-the-path-and-pedestri
 an-toronto-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
