BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AVANT MUTEK in Toronto in collaboration with LINK MUSIC LAB
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260530T210000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260531T030000
UID:blogto-233720@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/15/original_image23250a18-8e9f-4b32-96eb-ee53529faf
 37.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Toronto\, ON — May 30\, 2026 — Link Music Lab joins forces
  with MUTEK Montréal to present AVANT MUTEK Toronto\, a one-night event c
 elebrating forward-thinking electronic music and audiovisual performance.\
 nEvent Details\nEvent: AVANT MUTEK Toronto\nDate: Saturday\, May 30\, 2026
 \nTime: 9:00 PM – 3:00 AM\nLocation: MOOI Space - 75 Pelham Ave\, Toront
 o\nPresented by: MUTEK Montréal & Link Music Lab\nTaking place at MOOI Sp
 ace\, this immersive experience unfolds across two rooms within an intimat
 e warehouse setting\, bringing together artists and audiences at the foref
 ront of contemporary sound.\nPositioned as a prelude to the internationall
 y renowned MUTEK Montréal Festival\, AVANT MUTEK Toronto offers a glimpse
  into the exploratory spirit that defines the festival highlighting cuttin
 g-edge practices in electronic music\, digital art\, and live performance.
 \nMore than a showcase of experimental sound\, this Toronto edition reflec
 ts Link Music Lab’s ongoing commitment to platforming diverse artistic v
 oices. Rooted in its connection to diasporic communities\, the event highl
 ights the presence of Iranian artists whose work bridges cultural memory w
 ith contemporary electronic forms. Alongside this\, the inclusion of Indig
 enous artists from Toronto brings forward local perspectives that ground t
 he night in the land and its living histories.\nThis year’s curated line
 up features a range of local and international musical artists\, including
  Arc & Texture (Caleb Klager & Vanese Smith)\, Èbony\, NIMKII & Farbod Ma
 een\, Honeydrip\, Satoshi Tomii & Kamran Sadeghi\, Masayuki Tomita and Ora
 nge Moon each contributing to a sonic landscape rooted in experimentation 
 and innovation. Their visual artists include Karl Skene\, Andrew O’Conno
 r\, InterAccess artists\, Alex Maclen and CR34TE Montréal .\nAbout MUTEK\
 nFounded in 2000\, MUTEK has become a global platform dedicated to digital
  creativity in sound and audiovisual art\, known for presenting visionary 
 artists and fostering new forms of artistic expression.\nLearn more: https
 ://mutek.org\nWith AVANT MUTEK Toronto\, Link Music Lab continues its comm
 itment to supporting boundary-pushing music practices while cultivating me
 aningful connections between artists\, audiences\, and international netwo
 rks.\nAbout Link Music Lab\nFounded in 2009 by Mahmood “Moudy” Schrick
 er\, musician and ethnomusicologist\, Link Music Lab is a Toronto-based ar
 tist collective & not-for-profit that strives to be a catalyst for content
  creation\, bringing communities together through innovative and inclusive
  music.\nLearn more: https://www.linkmusiclab.com/about
LOCATION:MOOI Space
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/avant-mutek-in-toronto-in-collaboration-
 with-link-music-lab-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
