BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Curious Minds // Toronto: Cinema City
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T150000
UID:blogto-233554@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/13/original_imagecd94c896-5cf6-43d8-9b60-3517b28dfe
 4d.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Saturdays\, June 6 - 27 at 1:00 PM - 3:00 PM\nRegister for the
  full course and save! Register now >>\nToronto's history can be told thro
 ugh its movie theatres. From bustling neighbourhood cinemas and Yonge Stre
 et grindhouses\, experimental film co-ops\, to the corporate rise of multi
 plex chains and decades of censorship battles\, the city's screens have mi
 rrored its cultural\, social and political life. In Toronto: Cinema City\,
  journalist and film historian Eric Veillette will lead us through a four-
 part journey through Toronto's exhibition history\, uncovering the theatre
 s\, controversies\, and communities that shaped how Torontonians have watc
 hed movies for 130 years.\nAbout the speaker\nEric Veillette is a Toronto-
 based journalist specializing in Canadian film culture. His work regularly
  appears in The Globe and Mail\, Toronto Star and Spacing Magazine. He is 
 the editor of The Downtown Theatre\, a weekly newsletter dedicated to the 
 history of Toronto moviegoing. A former culture reporter for CBC/Radio-Can
 ada\, he is currently journalist-in-residence at York University's Archive
 /CounterArchive\, where he researches film censorship. From 2015-2020 he w
 as the programming director at The Revue Cinema. He’s also writing a boo
 k about Toronto’s cinemas and cinephile culture\, In the Dark\, to be pu
 blished by ECW Press in 2027.
LOCATION:Hot Docs Ted Rogers Cinema
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/curious-minds-toronto-cinema-city-toront
 o/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eritrean and Ethiopian Workers Meet-Up\, Mayworks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260606T170000
UID:blogto-233902@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/20/original_image09c07e68-90e8-44a6-bc80-163d60deb2
 ca.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A meet up led by the Ethiopian and Eritrean Workers Network of
  the Toronto and York Region Labour Council\nCalling all Eritrean and Ethi
 opian newcomers\, workers and community members! Join us for a community g
 athering and creative workshop. In search for opportunity\, many of us arr
 ived in Canada through great sacrifice\, leaving our dreams\, degrees\, fa
 milies\, and professions in Eritrea and Ethiopia. For many of our communit
 y members\, we are represented in working roles that are precarious and un
 protected. In this workshop\, we will learn to dramatize our stories and e
 xperiences into scenes that help us reflect on our relationship to work an
 d the power we hold. Together\, we will also discuss finding employment op
 portunities\, unions\, and knowing your rights in the workplace.\nFood and
  refreshments will be provided.
LOCATION:Spadina and Bloor
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/eritrean-and-ethiopian-workers-meet-up-m
 ayworks-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
