BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Anga's Farm: Seminar: Houseplants 101 for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T140000
UID:blogto-233372@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/04/09/original_image4e354087-ae0a-43ef-acc3-6678501ee0
 3c.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Houseplants 101: How to Choose (and Keep Alive) the Right Plan
 ts for Your Space\nNo green thumb? No problem. Houseplants 101 is a fun\, 
 beginner-friendly seminar that covers all the essentials of indoor plant c
 are and plant styling. Learn how to choose the right plants for your light
  conditions\, care for them properly\, and avoid the most common mistakes\
 , so you can fill your home with lush greenery with confidence.\nYou’ll 
 walk away with clarity\, practical knowledge\, and a new appreciation for 
 how plants can elevate your home. We’ll also highlight three great start
 er plants for bright\, medium\, and low-light spaces\, so no matter your s
 etup\, you’ll find something that thrives.\nFor more details & to sign u
 p\, visit our website www.angasfarm.ca
LOCATION:Anga's Farm & Nursery
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/angas-farm-seminar-houseplants-101-for-b
 eginners-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BIG on Bloor 20 - Bloordale's Festival of Art & Culture
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260718T210000
UID:blogto-232694@blogto.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://blogto-production2-baselayer-display.blo
 gto.com/events/2026/03/25/original_image9cd7d2b2-d9a1-4d5c-a0de-709d1af2c0
 44.jpg
DESCRIPTION:To mark its 20th anniversary\, BIG on Bloor will debut CEREMON
 Y\, a major new curatorial feature that transforms a neighbourhood side st
 reet into an immersive public art environment.\nInspired by multicultural 
 wedding traditions\, CEREMONY presents a series of interactive installatio
 ns and live performances that explore themes of connection\, ritual\, and 
 collective celebration. The project invites audiences to move through a ro
 tating program of artistic interpretations drawn from global matrimonial c
 ustoms.\nFestival attendees are invited to experience CEREMONY at this yea
 r's BIG on Bloor not just as spectators\, but as wedding guests.
URL:https://www.blogto.com/events/big-on-bloor-20-bloordales-festival-of-a
 rt-culture-toronto/
X-SOURCE:blogTO
